spans.s:
tādṛśaka,
(1) adj. (= Pali tādisaka), such, = Skt. tādṛśa: Mv 〔iii.287.10〕 (prose; correl. with yādṛśaka, q.v.);
(2) = BHS tādṛśa, and tāyin, q.v.; applied to a Bodhisattva or a Buddha; holy: (kausīdyaprāptas tada yo babhūva …) tvam eva so tādṛśako babhūva SP 〔28.2〕 (vs), addressed to the Bodhisattva Maitreya, (he who was indolent at that time …) has become none other than thou, the holy one (misunderstood by Burnouf and Kern); tvam eva so tādṛśako bhaviṣyasi anābhibhūto dvipadānam uttamaḥ SP 〔69.4〕 (vs), predicting Buddhahood in the future, thou thyself shalt become a Holy One (a Buddha), unconquered, best of bipeds.
